== D8: tasks, deadlocks

$ jet run cycle.jet
Stop: Jet.Deadlock: Tasks wait on each other
  --> cycle.jet:23
  task 3 (link)  waits to receive from a channel only task 1 and task 2 send on  cycle.jet:11
  task 1 (main)  waits to receive from a channel only task 1 and task 3 send on  cycle.jet:23
  task 2 (link)  waits to receive from a channel only task 1 sends on  cycle.jet:11
 Why: Each task of the cycle waits for the next one: to join it, to edit a Shared value it holds, or to receive on a channel only it can send on. The main task is one of them, so the program could never finish. The `-->` line is where the main task waits; each line below names a task, what it waits for and where.
 Fix: Break the cycle: send before you receive, join a task only after the values it waits for are sent, or give one wait a deadline or a `select` with another way out.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.Deadlock
(exit 70; wall 2910 ms, cpu 3814 ms, load 93.01 36.84 50.43)

