  --> crash.jet:9 in check
    |
9 |     if same && total > 20 -> panic("count too high: {total}")
    |                              ^^^^^
locals: count = 3, same = true, total = 21
 Why: The program hit a `panic`, `assert`, or `assert_eq` call that failed, a bounds/key check triggered at runtime, or another program-side stop. The shared report boundary owns the program-side stop; an unhandled entry error is a returned report, not Jet.Panic. Jet file and line are shown in Jet terms.
 Fix: Fix the logic that led to the failure. Program-side stops exit 70 through the shared boundary; unhandled entry errors print their report and exit 1; exit 101 is reserved for Jet defects.
More: jet-lang.dev/e/Jet.Panic
